To run the dsa application we need the following libraries pre installed
1) Install libmbedtls
	sudo apt-get install libmbedtls-dev

2) Install libjson-c
	sudo apt-get install libjson-c-dev

3) Link libmbedcrypto.so.1 to libmbedcrypto.so.0
   Example:
	sudo ln -s /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libmbedcrypto.so.1 /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libmbedcrypto.so.0

4) Link libjson-c.so to libjson-c.so.2
   Example:
	sudo ln -s /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libjson-c.so /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libjson-c.so.2

5) Copy seclib_data.json file to /etc/lucid/
	cp seclib_data.json /etc/lucid/.

6) Copy dsa_util to your prefered location.

7) Change file permissions on dsa_util
	chmod +x dsa_util

8) Run dsa_util help:
	$ ./dsa_util -h
	Usage: ./dsa_util [-e <ecu_id>] [-l <security level>] [-s <seed>]
	-h: display this information.
	-e: Ecu Id to use.
	-l: Security level.(1, 3, 7)
	-s: Seed

9) Run dsa_util.
   Example:
	$ ./dsa_util -e 9 -l 1 -s 1234567890abcdef
	key level 1
	Encrypt data is: ac24f9bad9cfd38326ae972d65dc8ee



